## Model Options

| Model Slug | Description | Best For |
|---|---|---|
| `composer-2.5-fast` | Fast variant of Composer 2.5 | Quick tasks, exploration, simple code generation |
| `composer-2.5` | Default Composer 2.5 | General-purpose tasks |
| `{ id: "auto" }` / `"auto"` | Server-resolved model | SDK integrations where server picks |

**Available models for subagents**: `composer-2.5-fast`

When not specifying a model, the system uses the default model for the account.

---

## Parallelism Patterns

### When to Use Parallel Execution

| Scenario | Parallel? | Reason |
|---|---|---|
| Independent file searches | Yes | No shared state, results don't depend on each other |
| Multiple codebase explorations | Yes | Read-only, independent queries |
| Best-of-N approaches | Yes | Each needs isolation |
| Sequential dependencies | No | Second task needs first task's output |
| Shared resource modification | No | Risk of conflicts |
| Git operations on same branch | No | Can cause lock contention |

### Parallel Launch Pattern

```
# All independent — launch in parallel
Task(description="Search for X", subagent_type="explore")
Task(description="Search for Y", subagent_type="explore")
Task(description="Search for Z", subagent_type="explore")
```

### Sequential Launch Pattern

```
# Dependent — launch sequentially
Task(description="Find all error handlers", subagent_type="explore")
→ Then, based on results:
Task(description="Refactor found error handlers", subagent_type="generalPurpose")
```

---

## Task Tool Parameters

| Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `description` | string | Yes | User-friendly title, appears in UI |
| `prompt` | string | Yes | Detailed task description with all context |
| `model` | string | No | Optional model slug |
| `resume` | string | No | Agent ID to resume, or `"self"` to fork |
| `readonly` | boolean | No | Default `false`. If `true`, agent cannot modify files |
| `subagent_type` | enum | Yes | One of: `generalPurpose`, `explore`, `shell`, `cursor-guide`, `ci-investigator`, `bugbot`, `security-review`, `best-of-n-runner` |
| `file_attachments` | string[] | No | Optional array of image/video file paths |
| `interrupt` | boolean | No | Default `false`. If `true` and `resume` targets a running async agent, interrupt and send new prompt |
| `run_in_background` | boolean | No | Default `false`. If `true`, agent runs independently |

